&lt;p&gt;Attentive is looking for a Senior People Business Partner to support our G&amp;amp;A and Marketing functions. This role will act as a strategic partner with leaders and executives, supporting these critical functions as our company scales. This role will report to the Director of People Business Partners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will need to be able to stay one step ahead of our growth and be able to coach and support our managers as we scale. As a Senior PBP at Attentive, you will play a significant role in the success of the teams you support. You will be an employee advocate, strategist, advisor, and coach and you will work closely with all levels of the organization to help build and support a high performing team. You will drive impact through coaching managers, managing performance, building strong relationships, and leading new initiatives. You will serve as a champion for Attentive’s values, ensuring People programs are delivering equitable experiences and outcomes across the organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Accomplish&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a trusted advisor and thought leader to managers and an advocate for employees&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide coaching and consultative support to employees &amp;amp; managers in the business units you support&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a strong business relationship with internal customers and the leadership team, partnering to drive people-centric strategies and programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with teams across the People organization to lead People cycles throughout the year including employee engagement surveys, compensation reviews, performance management, feedback cycles, and learning and development programming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive a high-performance culture and provoke positive change in people management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner and consult to build people plans for client groups, including career ladders, talent assessment and planning, organizational development and design, and engagement strategy development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively support and deliver People programs to the business in the areas of employee relations, training &amp;amp; development, performance management, onboarding/offboarding, change management and resource planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft and implement creative and progressive talent strategies, addressing retention and development needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be empathetic and thoughtful in your approach and will be obsessed with identifying areas of improvement and proposing and executing on solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will need to be forward thinking and creative to recommend and execute on people strategies to drive business outcomes and enable our team to be their best&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-7 years of progressive HR experience with a minimum of 3 years in an HRBP capacity in a high-growth and/or tech environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading and executing on large-scale change management within dynamic environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to drive through ambiguity and deliver solutions with autonomy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builder mentality with adaptability, flexibility, and a willingness to roll up your sleeves to ensure the right outcomes for our customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of developing, executing against, and measuring the success of people programs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about building and supporting strong teams with aggressive goals&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to effectively partner with cross-functional partners (e.g. Finance, Business Operations) and the broader People team to build a better employee experience for employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment; problem-solving skills are a must&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thoughtful discretion and hyper-sensitivity around confidential and sensitive information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire to learn and grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll get competitive&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.attentive.com/benefits&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;perks and benefits&lt;/a&gt;, from health &amp;amp; wellness to equity, to help you bring your best self to work.&lt;/p&gt;
