&lt;p&gt;The Product Analytics team is at the forefront of Attentive innovation, measuring results and delivering insight on new AI products. We are looking for a&amp;nbsp; Product Analyst to be the resident expert on Attentive AI, as well as other products. Product analysts at Attentive are strategic thought partners to the Product Management organization and Strategy teams. Responsibilities include measuring results &amp;amp; delivering insights on new products across their development lifecycle: experimentation, launch, post-launch and at scale. Product analysts help define the trajectory of new product launches, identify areas of opportunity within existing launches / mature products, and provide recommendations to product managers and the executive team to inform the product roadmap.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;This role is crucial to Attentive &amp;amp; our customers’ success and has high leadership visibility. Ideal candidates love breaking down complex problems, building solutions, delivering actionable and data-driven insights, and working in a fast-paced, dynamic environment.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Accomplish&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product managers &amp;amp; engineers to measure results of &amp;amp; deliver insight on products across their lifecycle: experimentation, launch, post-launch and at scaleIdentify key metrics and insights to track progress of highest priority initiatives including Attentive’s suite of new AI products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop analytics frameworks to run AB tests and measure the success of product features and initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uncover insights to help identify new product opportunities that maximize performance of marketing programs for Attentive customers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present recommendations to product organization &amp;amp; executive leadership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of relevant work experience in analytics, data science, or business intelligence with experiencing using a data visualization tool (Looker, Tableau,&amp;nbsp; Qlikview, MicroStrategy)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using, writing and optimizing SQL queries in a business environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of statistics and experience running A/B tests&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of data warehouse technical architecture, infrastructure components, ETL and reporting/analytic tools and environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to execute fast-paced and dynamic projects in a highly organized manner&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have an inherent curiosity and analytic follow-through; you can’t help but ask “why?” and love using data and logic to explore potential solutions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience effectively communicating the results of analyses with stakeholders to drive strategy decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Mathematics, Statistics, Finance, or equivalent work experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll get competitive&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.attentive.com/benefits&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;perks and benefits&lt;/a&gt;, from health &amp;amp; wellness to equity, to help you bring your best self to work.&lt;/p&gt;
